# oracle: pair_style body/rounded/polyhedron with friction mu 0.5 (no history): two rounded cubes approaching at speed 2 with a lateral sliding velocity, one cube turned 30 degrees about z and the other offset by 0.6 in y, fix nve/body, 2000 steps: thermo pe ke etotal press and the atom state
# Measured (engine vs native): thermo max relative error 7e-11 (press, 1.6e-6 in magnitude; pe and ke below 1e-14), per-atom state (x, v, f) max 1.8e-13 (fx). Friction is active: with mu 0 the vy of atom 1 is 0.33334 against 0.33335 with mu 0.5 at the end of the run. The torque sums of atom 1 (c_r1) are checked in the thermo columns.
# oracle-inputs: w121body_cubes_friction.data
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-12
units           lj
dimension       3
atom_style      body rounded/polyhedron 1 8
atom_modify     map array
read_data       w121body_cubes_friction.data
set             atom 1 vx 2.0 vy 0.5 vz 0.0
set             atom 2 vx -2.0 vy 0.0 vz 0.0
pair_style      body/rounded/polyhedron 20 5 0.5 1 0.5
pair_coeff      * * 100 1
comm_modify     vel yes
neighbor        0.5 bin
neigh_modify    every 1 delay 0 check yes
timestep        0.001
fix             1 all nve/body
group           g1 id 1
compute         t1 all property/atom tqx tqy tqz angmomx angmomy angmomz
compute         r1 g1 reduce sum c_t1[1] c_t1[2] c_t1[3] c_t1[4] c_t1[5] c_t1[6]
thermo_style    custom step pe ke etotal press c_r1[1] c_r1[2] c_r1[3] c_r1[4] c_r1[5] c_r1[6]
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          50
run             2000
